        "input": "This is a task from an agent benchmark. Can you return the `mapped_rxn` associated with the template that, when applied to the molecule below (provided as available input data), reproduces the reaction: In a cycloaddition reaction, two unsaturated molecules (or parts of the same molecule) combine to form a cyclic product. The reaction typically involves the formation of new sigma bonds between the reacting species, resulting in the creation of a ring structure. During the reaction, a carbon-carbon bond is formed, while a carbon-oxygen bond is broken. As a result of these transformations, a 'ketones' and 'C-C triple bonds' functional groups are lost.\n\nBelow are a few scenarios that may contain an agent's correct/incorrect thought-action pairs.\n\nWhich scenario corresponds to a correct/incorrect tought-action pair?",
        "target_scores": {
          "<thought>\nLet me analyze this task step by step:\n\n1. I have a molecule: COC(C1(C=C1[Si](C)(C)C)/C=C/C2=CC=CC=C2)=O\n2. The task describes a cycloaddition reaction (forward direction) where:\n   - Two unsaturated molecules combine to form a cyclic product\n   - A C-C bond is formed\n   - A C-O bond is broken\n   - Functional groups lost: 'ketones' and 'C-C triple bonds'\n\n3. Since I need to perform the retrosynthetic step (reverse of the forward reaction), I need to find a template that:\n   - In the forward direction: forms C-C bonds, breaks C-O bonds, and loses ketones and C-C triple bonds\n   - In the retrosynthetic direction: this would break the cyclic product back to precursors\n\nLet me start by searching for templates that match these criteria. I'll search for templates where:\n- bonds_formed: [\"6-6\"] (C-C bond formed in forward)\n- bonds_broken: [\"6-8\"] (C-O bond broken in forward, where 8 is oxygen)\n- functional_groups_broken: [\"ketones\", \"C-C triple bonds\"]\n</thought>\n\n<action>search_template_catalog_by_criteria</action>\n<action_input>\n{\n  \"molecule_smiles\": \"COC(C1(C=C1[Si](C)(C)C)/C=C/C2=CC=CC=C2)=O\",\n  \"functional_groups_broken\": [\"ketones\", \"C-C triple bonds\"],\n  \"bonds_formed\": [\"6-6\"],\n  \"bonds_broken\": [\"6-8\"],\n  \"limit\": 20\n}\n</action_input>": 1.0,
          "<thought>\nThe molecule contains carboxylic esters, C-C double bonds, and aromatic rings. \n\nNow let me search for templates based on the criteria described. For a retrosynthetic step:\n- In the forward reaction: C-C bond formed, C-O bond broken, ketones and C-C triple bonds lost\n- For retrosynthesis (reverse): \n  - bonds_broken should be C-C (what was formed in forward)\n  - bonds_formed should be C-O (what was broken in forward)\n  - functional_groups_formed should include ketones and C-C triple bonds (what was lost in forward)\n\nLet me search the template catalog with these criteria.\n</thought>\n\n<action>search_template_catalog_by_criteria</action>\n<action_input>{\n  \"molecule_smiles\": \"COC(C1(C=C1[Si](C)(C)C)/C=C/C2=CC=CC=C2)=O\",\n  \"bonds_broken\": [\"6-6\"],\n  \"bonds_formed\": [\"6-8\"],\n  \"functional_groups_formed\": [\"ketones\", \"C-C triple bonds\"],\n  \"limit\": 20\n}</action_input>": 0.0,
          "<thought>\nNo results with those specific criteria. Let me try a broader search. Maybe I should focus on the key aspects:\n- functional_groups_formed: ketones and C-C triple bonds (these are lost in forward, so formed in retro)\n- bonds_broken: C-C bond (formed in forward, broken in retro)\n\nLet me try without specifying bonds_formed.\n</thought>\n\n<action>search_template_catalog_by_criteria</action>\n<action_input>{\n  \"molecule_smiles\": \"COC(C1(C=C1[Si](C)(C)C)/C=C/C2=CC=CC=C2)=O\",\n  \"bonds_broken\": [\"6-6\"],\n  \"functional_groups_formed\": [\"ketones\", \"C-C triple bonds\"],\n  \"limit\": 20\n}</action_input>": 0.0,
